---
title: "Production Machining Techniques"
code: "MAC-206"
category: "machine-technology"
credits: "6"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Offers practice in advanced machine shop. Emphasizes mass production techniques and interchangeable parts manufacture. Covers setup and operation of tooling and fixtures to manufacture workpieces to specified tolerances. Lecture 4 hours. Laboratory 6 hours. Total 10 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
